<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mpu Kanwa</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">11th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mpu Kanwa was a court poet of King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/airlangga">Airlangga</a> of Kahuripan in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-java">East Java</a> in the early 11th century. He wrote the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arjunawiwaha">Arjunawiwaha</a>, composed around 1030, one of the earliest and most admired <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/old-javanese">Old Javanese</a> kakawin poems. Drawing on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mahabharata">Mahabharata</a>, the poem is widely read as an allegory of Airlangga's own trials and victory.</p></div>
